::ENG2_U05_L01_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Draft: "When the library closes early." Which revision fixes the fragment?{
=A. When the library closes early, students lose a quiet place to work.#Correct. This revision adds a complete thought to the dependent clause.
~B. When the library closes early and.#Incorrect. This is still incomplete.
~C. When the library.#Incorrect. This is still a fragment.
~D. Library closes early when.#Incorrect. This is unclear and incomplete.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Draft: "Some students ride late buses, they need a safe place to study." Which revision fixes the run-on?{
~A. Some students ride late buses, they need a safe place to study.#Incorrect. This keeps the comma splice.
=B. Some students ride late buses, so they need a safe place to study.#Correct. The word "so" correctly shows the relationship between the ideas.
~C. Some students ride late buses they need a safe place to study.#Incorrect. This removes punctuation and keeps the run-on problem.
~D. Some students ride late buses, safe study.#Incorrect. This is unclear.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.V.01] Which revision replaces vague wording with precise academic vocabulary?{
~A. The library is good.#Incorrect. "Good" is vague.
~B. The library is a place.#Incorrect. This is still vague.
=C. The library provides a quiet and reliable study space.#Correct. This revision uses precise wording that explains the library's value.
~D. The library is nice and stuff.#Incorrect. This is informal and vague.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which sentence best fits an audience of school leaders?{
~A. You should keep the library open because it is cool.#Incorrect. This is informal.
~B. The library thing should stay open.#Incorrect. This is vague.
~C. Everyone knows the library is good.#Incorrect. This is unsupported and imprecise.
=D. Keeping the library open after school would give students a quiet and supervised place to complete assignments.#Correct. This sentence is clear, specific, and audience-appropriate.
}

::ENG2_U05_L01_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence uses correct punctuation?{
~A. The library should stay open, students need a quiet place.#Incorrect. This is a comma splice.
=B. The library should stay open because students need a quiet place.#Correct. This sentence joins the reason correctly.
~C. The library should stay open students need a quiet place.#Incorrect. This is a run-on.
~D. Because students need a quiet place.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
}
